# GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 (react-router, via react-router-dom@7.18.0): CSRF bypass
# in "unstable RSC" (React Server Components) code paths only. This app is a
# Vite SPA using react-router-dom with BrowserRouter and does not use any
# unstable_RSC APIs, so it is not exploitable here. Fixed version (8.3.0)
# requires migrating off react-router-dom (merged into react-router in v8).
# Revisit when doing a planned react-router major-version upgrade.
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2

# GHSA-w3rx-r6r6-pgpr / GHSA-5p2g-fcmc-qvqq (image-size, via
# pptxgenjs@4.0.1): denial-of-service via infinite loop when parsing
# malformed ICNS/JXL/HEIF image headers. image-size is used here only to
# read dimensions of images the app itself embeds into generated
# PowerPoint exports (client/src, pptxgenjs export path) - it never
# parses images from untrusted/external input, so the DoS is not
# reachable in this app's usage. No patched image-size release exists yet;
# the only current fix path is `npm audit fix --force`, which downgrades
# pptxgenjs 4.0.1 -> 1.1.5 (major breaking regression). Revisit once
# image-size/pptxgenjs ship a real fix.
# Trivy's DB now surfaces these same two advisories under CVE IDs instead
# of (or alongside) their GHSA IDs - listing both forms so a DB refresh
# choosing either identifier still gets suppressed.
GHSA-w3rx-r6r6-pgpr
GHSA-5p2g-fcmc-qvqq
CVE-2025-71329
CVE-2025-71330

# CVE-2026-14257 / GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg (brace-expansion memory-exhaustion DoS):
# the GHSA advisory only lists 5.0.8 as "patched" and doesn't record the
# maintainer's backport releases for older major lines. client/package.json's
# overrides pin brace-expansion to 1.1.17 (under minimatch@3.1.5) and 2.1.3
# (under minimatch@5.1.9) - both verified by inspecting the published tarball
# to contain the actual fix (EXPANSION_MAX_LENGTH bound, same code as 5.0.8)
# while keeping the old callable-function export those minimatch versions
# require. Forcing 5.0.8 there instead breaks at runtime: 5.0.8 changed the
# export from a function to an object ({ expand, ... }), which minimatch@3.x/
# 5.x (pulled in transitively via exceljs -> archiver -> glob/readdir-glob)
# cannot consume. Re-check if exceljs/archiver ever bump their glob/minimatch
# versions.
CVE-2026-14257
